## How to work here

Skills in `{{.SkillsDir}}/` explain everything specific to this setup. Read the
relevant one before acting:

- `ror2-mod-workflow`: build, install into the game, launch, read logs. Read first.
- `ror2-game-code`: look up the game's real classes and assets instead of guessing.
- `ror2-content-recipes`: items, buffs, stats, equipment, settings with R2API.
- `ror2-thunderstore-release`: versioning and packaging for Thunderstore.

## Commands

```sh
ror2 dev build        # compile (fix all errors)
ror2 dev deploy       # build + install into the game as a dev mod
ror2 dev log          # this mod's log lines and errors from the last launch
ror2 dev decompile RoR2.CharacterBody   # read game code
ror2 launch           # start the game (ask the person first)
ror2 dev package      # Thunderstore zip in build/
```

## Ground rules

- The game runs through Wine on macOS; there is no debugger. Test by deploying,
  launching and reading `ror2 dev log`.
- Verify game APIs with `ror2 dev decompile` before using them. Many members were
  renamed or obsoleted in recent game updates.
- Gameplay changes only when `NetworkServer.active` (host).
- Keep the version identical in `Plugin.cs`, `{{.Name}}.csproj` and `manifest.json`.
- Never edit files inside the game folder directly; use `ror2 dev deploy`.
- Commit to git after each working step.
- The person may not be a programmer: explain what you changed and how to try it
  in plain language, and say what they should see in-game.
